      "img": "systems/pf2e/assets/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
      "name": "Impossible Grip",
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "sort": 450000,
      "system": {
        "_migration": {
          "previous": {
            "foundry": "13.351",
            "schema": 0.933,
            "system": "7.7.4"
          },
          "version": 0.953
        },
        "actionType": {
          "value": "passive"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>When a creature is Grabbed by a Tentacle, that creature can <strong>not</strong> attempt to Escape using the basic @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.SkZAQRkLLkmBQNB9]{Escape} action. A creature that is Restrained by a Tentacle can attempt to Escape, but a successful Escape results in the creature being Grabbed, not freed.</p><p>When a tentacle is brought to half HP, any creature currently grabbed by it can attempt to make a single special Escape check as a free action. The ally who brought the tentacle to the HP threshold is considered to have taken sufficient preparation to use their reaction to Aid.</p><p>Allies of a grabbed player can help them escape by Shoving the grabbed player, as a grabbed player affected by forced movement will break the grab as normal.</p><p>If a Tentacle has a creature Grabbed, it does not lose the Grabbed condition at the end of the Tentacle's next turn. It remains Grabbed until it Escapes or the Tentacle is destroyed. If a Tentacle has a creature Restrained, the Restrained condition is reduced to Grabbed at the end of the Tentacle's next turn.</p><p data-visibility=\"gm\">You should allow abilities such as Liberating Command or Freedom of Movement to allow characters to Escape as normal.</p>"
        },
        "publication": {
          "authors": "",
          "license": "OGL",
          "remaster": false,
          "title": ""
        },
