          },
          "version": 0.953
        },
        "actionType": {
          "value": "passive"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>Tentacles do not get their own turn, they act at the end of Scylladon's turn, similar to minions with the Independent feat.</p><p>Each Tentacle gains two actions per round.</p><p>Its first action can only be used to Swim higher or lower if it isn't in reach of a creature.</p><p>Its second action can only be used to make an Athletics check to Grapple a creature within 10 feet, or, if it already has a creature grabbed, it uses this second action to use Crushing Grip instead.</p><p>Because Tentacles extend from the floor, they can be attacked from any square beneath them while they are \"swimming\" at a higher elevation.</p><p>If a Tentacle is holding an unconscious target at the start of its turn, it will release that target.</p><p>Only one Tentacle at a time may grapple a target; if the only available target is already in another Tentacles grasp, the Tentacle does nothing.</p>"
        },
